[436.109511, "o", "\r\u2838 Thinking...          "]
[436.12184, "o", "\r                                        \r\r\nI've researched ntfy and put together a `WORKLOAD.md` with my findings. Here is the summary:\r\n\r\n**ntfy** is a lightweight, HTTP-based pub-sub notification service written in Go. Although it's a Go app, it relies heavily on persistent local storage (embedded SQLite databases for caching and users, plus local directories for attachments). Because it requires durable storage to avoid losing messages and user accounts on restarts, deploying it as a stateless 12-factor app isn't the best fit.\r\n\r\nInstead, I propose we build a **Custom Kubernetes Charm** (Path B) that wraps the official upstream Docker image (`binwiederhier/ntfy`) and provisions Juju storage for persistence.\r\n\r\n### Proposed Design\r\n\r\n*   **Substrate:** Kubernetes\r\n*   **Charm Path:** Custom Application (using the official OCI image)\r\n*   **OCI Image:** `binwiederhier/ntfy` (we can look up the latest specific tag)\r\n*   **Storage:**\r\n    *   `data`: Mapped to `/var/cache/ntfy` (for the message cache and attachments)\r\n    *   `config`: Mapped to `/etc/ntfy` (for `user.db` and configuration)\r\n*   **Networking:** Exposes HTTP on port 80.\r\n*   **Config Options:**\r\n    *   `base-url`: The external URL of the server (e.g., `https://ntfy.example.com`).\r\n    *   `auth-default-access`: Whether to allow anonymous access (`read-write`, `read-only`, `write-only`, `deny-all`).\r\n    *   `log-level`: `INFO`, `DEBUG`, etc.\r\n*   **Integrations:**\r\n    *   `ingress`: To route external traffic to ntfy via Traefik.\r\n    *   `cos`: For metrics, logs, and dashboards.\r\n\r\nHow does this design look to you? Are there any other config options, specific storage sizes, or integrations you'd like to add before we start building?\r\n\r\n"]
[436.125041, "o", "> "]
